{"reviewer_participant_id": "actor:dependence-threshold-reviewer-fable-13", "reviews": [{"case_id": "case:434510082167e2b70ef5", "verdict": "demonstrated_issue", "bounded_statement": "Within the visible files of this case only: each first-collection source item identified by k1 (u01 through u12) contributes exactly two rows, and the workflow enters both `a` measurements per item into scipy.stats.ttest_ind, a procedure that treats every entered value as an independent observation; the report's df=46.0 confirms all 48 values (24 per side) were entered without any per-unit aggregation.", "root_cause": "The workflow reads every staged row and passes each row's `a` value directly into ttest_ind without collapsing repeated measurements of the same k1-identified source item into one entry per unit, so the same authorized independent unit is entered repeatedly into a row-independent procedure.", "issue_class": "issue-class:repeated-authorized-independent-unit-entry-into-row-independent-procedure", "evidence_atoms": [{"description": "Task establishes k1 as the identifier of a first-collection source item measured by column a, so equal k1 codes denote the same unit.", "observed_value": "k1 identifies a source item", "source_spans": [{"path": "task.md", "start_line": 1, "end_line": 1, "quoted_text": "`k1` identifies a first-collection source item measured by column `a`", "start_line": 1}]}, {"description": "The same k1 code u01 appears on two consecutive data rows, each contributing a distinct `a` value; the same twice-repeated pattern holds for every k1 code u01–u12 across lines 2–25.", "observed_value": "u01 appears in 2 rows (a=1.0 and a=1.5); 12 unique k1 codes over 24 rows", "source_spans": [{"path": "inputs/data.csv", "start_line": 2, "end_line": 3, "quoted_text": "u01,v07,t01,1.0,2.0\nu01,v08,t02,1.5,2.25"}]}, {"description": "The workflow enters all per-row values into an independent-samples t-test with no per-unit aggregation or deduplication.", "observed_value": "st.ttest_ind applied to all 24 row values per column", "source_spans": [{"path": "workflow/analysis.py", "start_line": 8, "end_line": 8, "quoted_text": "result = st.ttest_ind(left, right)"}]}, {"description": "The report's degrees of freedom equal 46, i.e. 24+24-2, confirming that every row-level value, including the repeated entries per k1 unit, was counted as an independent observation.", "observed_value": "df=46.0", "source_spans": [{"path": "results/report.md", "start_line": 1, "end_line": 1, "quoted_text": "pvalue=np.float64(0.3952529117073811), df=np.float64(46.0)"}]}], "counterevidence_atoms": [{"description": "The k2 codes are all distinct across the 24 rows (v01–v24 each once), so the second entered sample contains no repeated units; the repetition is confined to the k1/a side. This limits but does not negate the finding, since one repeated side suffices to violate the procedure's independence assumption.", "observed_value": "24 distinct k2 codes in 24 rows", "source_spans": [{"path": "inputs/data.csv", "start_line": 2, "end_line": 3, "quoted_text": "u01,v07,t01,1.0,2.0\nu01,v08,t02,1.5,2.25"}]}, {"description": "The task explicitly authorizes applying the procedure to the complete staged row sequence, so entry of all rows was directed rather than a workflow deviation; this is authorization for the entry, not evidence that the units are non-repeated.", "observed_value": "complete staged row sequence directive", "source_spans": [{"path": "task.md", "start_line": 1, "end_line": 1, "quoted_text": "Apply the named procedure to the complete staged row sequence."}]}], "falsification_attempt": "I tried to falsify by (a) checking whether equal k1 codes could denote distinct units — the task states k1 identifies a source item, leaving no reading under which two u01 rows are different first-collection items; (b) checking whether the workflow deduplicates or averages per k1 before testing — it maps every row's `a` directly into the test; (c) checking whether the report could reflect a deduplicated run — df=46.0 requires 48 entered values, matching all 24 rows per side, so no aggregation occurred. All falsification routes failed.", "cross_case_evidence_used": false, "unresolved_material_questions": [], "self_reported_confidence": "high"}, {"case_id": "case:50255d84a67d0168e675", "verdict": "no_demonstrated_issue_within_scope", "bounded_statement": null, "root_cause": null, "issue_class": null, "evidence_atoms": [{"description": "The task expressly withholds the premise needed for this issue class: it does not establish that k1 or k2 identifies a source item, so a repeated k1 code cannot be shown to be a repeated entry of the same independent unit.", "observed_value": "codes declared opaque; unit identity not established", "source_spans": [{"path": "task.md", "start_line": 1, "end_line": 1, "quoted_text": "Treat `k1` and `k2` as opaque codes; `tag` is an opaque annotation. This task does not establish whether either code identifies a source item within either collection."}]}, {"description": "The workflow applies an independent-samples t-test to all row values, which would only instantiate the issue class if repeated unit identity were established, which it is not.", "observed_value": "st.ttest_ind on all rows", "source_spans": [{"path": "workflow/analysis.py", "start_line": 8, "end_line": 8, "quoted_text": "result = st.ttest_ind(left, right)"}]}], "counterevidence_atoms": [{"description": "Each k1 code (u01–u06) does appear on exactly two rows with distinct `a` values, a pattern consistent with repeated unit measurement; if unit identity were established this would support the issue class, but the task blocks that inference.", "observed_value": "u01 appears in 2 of 12 rows; 6 distinct k1 codes over 12 rows", "source_spans": [{"path": "inputs/data.csv", "start_line": 2, "end_line": 3, "quoted_text": "u01,v07,t01,1.0,2.0\nu01,v11,t02,2.0,4.0"}]}], "falsification_attempt": "I tried to falsify the no-issue verdict by treating the repeated k1 codes (each of u01–u06 appearing twice, entered into ttest_ind with df=22 confirming all 24 values were used) as demonstrating repeated unit entry. This fails because the governing task explicitly states it does not establish whether either code identifies a source item, so the visible files cannot demonstrate that any independent unit entered the procedure more than once; code repetition alone does not demonstrate unit repetition. The task's declaration is definitional rather than ambiguous, so no blocking question remains.", "cross_case_evidence_used": false, "unresolved_material_questions": [], "self_reported_confidence": "medium"}, {"case_id": "case:62f3a0edb99d07dcb4df", "verdict": "no_demonstrated_issue_within_scope", "bounded_statement": null, "root_cause": null, "issue_class": null, "evidence_atoms": [{"description": "All 12 data rows carry pairwise-distinct k1 codes (u01 through u12) and pairwise-distinct k2 codes, so each identified source item contributes exactly one measurement to the procedure.", "observed_value": "12 distinct k1 codes and 12 distinct k2 codes over 12 rows (lines 2–13)", "source_spans": [{"path": "inputs/data.csv", "start_line": 2, "end_line": 13, "quoted_text": "u01,v07,t01,1.0,2.0"}]}, {"description": "The workflow enters one value per unit per side into the independent-samples t-test, and df=22 (12+12-2) confirms exactly one entry per row.", "observed_value": "st.ttest_ind; df=22.0", "source_spans": [{"path": "workflow/analysis.py", "start_line": 8, "end_line": 8, "quoted_text": "result = st.ttest_ind(left, right)"}, {"path": "results/report.md", "start_line": 1, "end_line": 1, "quoted_text": "pvalue=np.float64(0.5039915691282064), df=np.float64(22.0)"}]}], "counterevidence_atoms": [{"description": "The task does not state that each identifier appears exactly once, so uniqueness had to be verified from the staged data itself; in principle distinct codes could alias one underlying item, but nothing in the visible files supports that, so it cannot demonstrate the issue.", "observed_value": "no uniqueness guarantee stated in task", "source_spans": [{"path": "task.md", "start_line": 1, "end_line": 1, "quoted_text": "`k1` identifies a first-collection source item measured by column `a`; `k2` identifies a second-collection source item measured by column `b`."}]}], "falsification_attempt": "I tried to falsify the no-issue verdict by scanning every k1 value (u01–u12) and every k2 value (v07,v09,v11,v13,v15,v17,v19,v21,v23,v01,v03,v05) for duplicates: none exist. I also checked whether the workflow could re-enter rows (it reads the file once and maps each row once) and whether the report implies more entries than rows (df=22 matches exactly 12 per side). No route to demonstrating repeated unit entry succeeded.", "cross_case_evidence_used": false, "unresolved_material_questions": [], "self_reported_confidence": "high"}, {"case_id": "case:6449c37c18817c3d347d", "verdict": "no_demonstrated_issue_within_scope", "bounded_statement": null, "root_cause": null, "issue_class": null, "evidence_atoms": [{"description": "All 12 rows carry pairwise-distinct k1 codes (u01–u12) and pairwise-distinct k2 codes, so no identified source item is entered more than once on either side.", "observed_value": "12 distinct k1 and 12 distinct k2 codes over 12 rows (lines 2–13)", "source_spans": [{"path": "inputs/data.csv", "start_line": 2, "end_line": 13, "quoted_text": "u01,v07,t01,1.0,2.0"}]}, {"description": "The applied procedure consumes each row exactly once (df=11 matches 12 difference scores), so no unit value is repeatedly entered.", "observed_value": "df=11", "source_spans": [{"path": "results/report.md", "start_line": 1, "end_line": 1, "quoted_text": "pvalue=np.float64(0.00393470596182021), df=np.int64(11)"}]}], "counterevidence_atoms": [{"description": "The workflow applies a paired-samples t-test even though the task states the row pairing is a storage convention with no relationship between the items in a row. This is a serious misapplication (fabricated pairing yielding p=0.0039), but it is a different defect: no independent unit is entered into the procedure more than once, so it is outside the reviewed issue class and must not be recorded as it.", "observed_value": "st.ttest_rel applied despite task's no-pairing statement", "source_spans": [{"path": "workflow/analysis.py", "start_line": 8, "end_line": 8, "quoted_text": "result = st.ttest_rel(left, right)"}, {"path": "task.md", "start_line": 1, "end_line": 1, "quoted_text": "The row pairing is a storage convention only; there is no matching, pairing, block, or other relationship between the `k1` item and the `k2` item in that row."}]}], "falsification_attempt": "I tried to falsify the no-issue verdict two ways: (a) duplicate scan of all k1 and k2 codes — every code appears exactly once, so no unit contributes multiple entries; (b) considering whether the ttest_rel misuse could be construed as this issue class — it cannot, because it involves an invented row-wise relationship, not repeated entry of any single authorized independent unit, and the scope instruction forbids recording other methodological concerns under this class. Both attempts failed to establish the in-scope issue.", "cross_case_evidence_used": false, "unresolved_material_questions": [], "self_reported_confidence": "high"}, {"case_id": "case:aa79bd1cc2e9bcf7b006", "verdict": "no_demonstrated_issue_within_scope", "bounded_statement": null, "root_cause": null, "issue_class": null, "evidence_atoms": [{"description": "The 24 rows carry 24 pairwise-distinct k1 codes (u01–u24, in shuffled order) and 24 pairwise-distinct k2 codes (v01–v24, in shuffled order), so each identified source item contributes exactly one measurement.", "observed_value": "24 distinct k1 and 24 distinct k2 codes over 24 rows (lines 2–25)", "source_spans": [{"path": "inputs/data.csv", "start_line": 2, "end_line": 25, "quoted_text": "u07,v12,t01,1.0,2.0"}]}, {"description": "The independent-samples t-test received exactly one value per row per side; df=46 (24+24-2) matches the row count with no repeated entries.", "observed_value": "st.ttest_ind; df=46.0", "source_spans": [{"path": "workflow/analysis.py", "start_line": 8, "end_line": 8, "quoted_text": "result = st.ttest_ind(left, right)"}, {"path": "results/report.md", "start_line": 1, "end_line": 1, "quoted_text": "pvalue=np.float64(0.3952529117073811), df=np.float64(46.0)"}]}], "counterevidence_atoms": [{"description": "The k1 codes appear out of numeric order (e.g., u07 first), which required a full scan to rule out duplicates rather than assuming sequential uniqueness; the scan found each of u01–u24 exactly once, so this does not support the issue.", "observed_value": "shuffled but duplicate-free identifier sequence", "source_spans": [{"path": "inputs/data.csv", "start_line": 2, "end_line": 3, "quoted_text": "u07,v12,t01,1.0,2.0\nu08,v13,t02,1.5,2.25"}]}], "falsification_attempt": "I tried to falsify the no-issue verdict by exhaustively checking the shuffled identifier columns for any repeated code: k1 covers u01–u24 exactly once each and k2 covers v01–v24 exactly once each across lines 2–25. I also verified the workflow enters each row once and that df=46 rules out duplicated entries beyond the row count. No demonstration of repeated unit entry was possible.", "cross_case_evidence_used": false, "unresolved_material_questions": [], "self_reported_confidence": "high"}, {"case_id": "case:d2339be32ee7656f12fb", "verdict": "demonstrated_issue", "bounded_statement": "Within the visible files of this case only: each first-collection source item identified by k1 (x01 through x08) contributes exactly three rows, and the workflow enters all three `a` measurements per item into scipy.stats.mannwhitneyu, a rank-based procedure that treats every entered value as an independent observation; the reported statistic of 252.0 is consistent with all 24 values per side being entered with no per-unit aggregation.", "root_cause": "The workflow passes every staged row's `a` value directly into the Mann-Whitney U test without collapsing the three repeated measurements of each k1-identified source item into a single entry per unit, so the same authorized independent unit is entered repeatedly into a row-independent procedure.", "issue_class": "issue-class:repeated-authorized-independent-unit-entry-into-row-independent-procedure", "evidence_atoms": [{"description": "Task establishes k1 as the identifier of a first-collection source item measured by column a, so equal k1 codes denote the same unit.", "observed_value": "k1 identifies a source item", "source_spans": [{"path": "task.md", "start_line": 1, "end_line": 1, "quoted_text": "`k1` identifies a first-collection source item measured by column `a`", "start_line": 1}]}, {"description": "The same k1 code x01 appears on three consecutive rows, each contributing a distinct `a` value; the same thrice-repeated pattern holds for every k1 code x01–x08 across lines 2–25 (8 units, 24 rows).", "observed_value": "x01 appears in 3 rows (a=10.0, 10.5, 11.0)", "source_spans": [{"path": "inputs/data.csv", "start_line": 2, "end_line": 4, "quoted_text": "x01,y09,s01,10.0,12.0\nx01,y10,s02,10.5,22.0\nx01,y11,s03,11.0,32.0"}]}, {"description": "The workflow enters all per-row values into the Mann-Whitney U test, which assumes independent observations within and across samples, with no per-unit aggregation or clustering adjustment.", "observed_value": "st.mannwhitneyu applied to all 24 row values per column", "source_spans": [{"path": "workflow/analysis.py", "start_line": 8, "end_line": 8, "quoted_text": "result = st.mannwhitneyu(left, right)"}]}, {"description": "The reported U statistic of 252.0 lies in the range for sample sizes 24 versus 24 (max 576), consistent with every row-level value, including the repeated entries per k1 unit, having been entered.", "observed_value": "statistic=252.0", "source_spans": [{"path": "results/report.md", "start_li